# The sites of the fast-test budget that exist today (scripts/check-test-budget.sh, test/README.md "Test budget"): KIND<TAB>NAME<TAB>COUNT<TAB>REASON.
#   unit   a test/unit/*.c with ROWS above 4000 or fuzz/rounds above 500 and no sanitizer branch; COUNT is the number of constants
#   sql    a test/sql/*.sql with generate_series above 50000 rows and no comment that says why; COUNT is the number of calls
#   slow   the names in SLOW_REGRESS (scripts/ci/weights.sh)
# A row only goes down: a count that grew or a new site fails, a row whose site was fixed is deleted (scripts/check-test-budget.sh --list prints the rows of the tree as it is).
